# Review & Fix Discipline

## Fix the Pattern, Not Just the Instance

When a reviewer flags a bug, search the entire codebase for all instances of the same
pattern before marking the comment resolved. A point fix that leaves identical bugs
elsewhere is incomplete.

## Propagate Fixes to All Implementations

If a core type, interface, or shared function changes, every dependent type and call
site must also be updated in the same PR. Do not leave stale signatures or casts behind.

## Regression Test with Every Fix

Every bug fix must include a test that would have caught the bug. If you cannot write
such a test, document why in the PR description.

## Zero Lint Warnings Policy

Fix ALL lint warnings before committing — including pre-existing warnings in files you
touched. Leaving warnings for later means they never get fixed.

## Mechanical Verification Before Committing

Before pushing, run this checklist:

1. Run the linter — zero warnings.
2. Grep changed files for common anti-patterns (hardcoded secrets, TODO/FIXME without
   issue links, disabled tests).
3. If you fixed a pattern bug, grep the repo for other instances of the same pattern.

## UTF-8 String Safety

Never use byte-index slicing on user-supplied or external strings. Use your language's
unicode-aware string operations (grapheme clusters, code points, or equivalent) to avoid
splitting multi-byte characters.

## Case-Insensitive Comparisons

When comparing user-supplied strings — file paths, media types, header names, locale
codes — normalize case before comparison. Do not assume input casing is consistent.

## Sensitive Data in Logs

Function parameters, return values, and intermediate state must be redacted before
logging or broadcasting. Never log tokens, passwords, PII, or full request/response
bodies in production log levels.

## Test Temporary Files

Use your language's temp-directory facilities (`mktemp`, `tempfile`, `os.tmpdir()`,
etc.) for any files created during tests. Never hardcode paths like `/tmp/mytest` —
they collide in parallel runs and break on other platforms.
